- Story & Context: Old Finn, the last seal hunter of the coastal village, confessed his recurring dream to the young cartographer: a spectral thread of warmth slowly pulled from his chest by an invisible hand, leaving him colder with each beat, knowing it was the ocean claiming its due; "Each breath you take, it's a fraying."
